  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/kpi-card/v1 (the stat/KPI card, 4th Alpine template). Standalone Alpine flavor: muted metric label, a dominant COUNT-UP value, a soft DELTA PILL (SVG-triangle arrow + signed change on a tinted rounded badge — green up / red down / muted flat), a muted sublabel, and an optional bottom SPARKLINE (soft area + line, reusing the line-chart geometry math). Mirrors the proven charts/stat-card patterns (triangle SVG mask not a tofu glyph; animateNumbersInText count-up; cascade fades) but owns the Alpine card chrome + palette + the pill + sparkline. Animation: value counts up, then the pill + sublabel cascade-fade, sparkline fades up — low flat tile count (≤10), shallow overlay depth (≤3), so no executor stress and no depth-limit risk. Verified 9 edge cases valid (down/flat/no-delta/no-spark/with-title/plain-value/empty); end + mid (count-up at $30,154, pill not yet in) frames clean. Dual props: Animate / Intro length → anim. NOTE on layout: value is left-aligned (hero style), leaving right-side whitespace that the full-width sparkline balances.",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine KPI card. Scrub it — value counts up, pill + sublabel cascade in, sparkline fills the bottom. Does the look land (label/value scale, the delta pill, sparkline softness, overall balance)? Open questions if you have a preference: (1) the value's right-side whitespace — keep hero-left, or add something there / center it? (2) sparkline on by default, or opt-in? I'll iterate one nudge at a time."
  }
